  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted, acc=72.5%), the key uncertainty is whether the RNA encoder choice is a bottleneck or a strength. config_043 changes only the RNA encoder from scvi_n200 to scgpt while holding all other variables constant (multimodal, multiprofile, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted). This isolates the effect of the RNA representation: scgpt (a generative masked-model encoder) vs scvi_n200 (a variational autoencoder). If scgpt outperforms, it signals the RNA modality is the limiting factor and I should explore more scgpt variants; if it underperforms, it confirms scvi_n200 is well-chosen and I should pivot to optimizing the image encoder or aggregation. This is the highest-information single-variable test available and will efficiently direct the remaining 8 experiments toward the most promising design axis."
}

